+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "toolChoice: 'required',",
+  "cause": "The refundAgent sets toolChoice to 'required', which forces the model to call a tool on every turn, so after approveRefund returns a decline it cannot send a text reply and instead keeps calling tools until maxTurns is exhausted.",
+  "evidence": "Reproducing the flow (refundAgent.chat().send(...), then resuming the approveRefund interrupt with approved: false) threw 'ABORTED: Exceeded maximum tool call iterations (6)' before the fix; after changing it to 'auto' the same run returns finishReason 'stop' with the text \"I'm sorry, your refund for order A-1001 was not approved because it is a duplicate claim.\" in repeated runs, and the approved path still issues refund R-1001. The triage agent already uses toolChoice 'auto' and the Genkit Google GenAI plugin maps 'required' to a forced function-calling mode."
+}
